 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# DataLabel.has_text_frame property not working correctly\n\n## Description\nWhen checking if a data label has a text frame using the `has_text_frame` property, it returns incorrect results. The property is using an attribute `has_tx_rich` that doesn't exist on the dLbl object, causing the property to fail.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\nfrom pptx.chart.data import CategoryChartData\n\n# Create a presentation with a chart\nprs = Presentation()\nslide = prs.slides.add_slide(prs.slide_layouts[5])\nchart_data = CategoryChartData()\nchart_data.categories = ['East', 'West', 'Midwest']\nchart_data.add_series('Series 1', (19.2, 21.4, 16.7))\nx, y, cx, cy = 2, 2, 6, 4\nchart = slide.shapes.add_chart(\n    chart_type=3, x=x, y=y, cx=cx, cy=cy, chart_data=chart_data\n).chart\n\n# Try to access data label text frame\npoint = chart.series[0].points[0]\ndata_label = point.data_label\nprint(data_label.has_text_frame)  # Should return True/False but raises AttributeError\n```\n\n## Expected Results\nThe `has_text_frame` property should correctly return True or False based on whether the data label has a text frame.\n\n## Actual Results\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"example.py\", line 19, in <module>\n    print(data_label.has_text_frame)\n  File \"/path/to/pptx/chart/datalabel.py\", line 180, in has_text_frame\n    return dLbl.has_tx_rich\nAttributeError: 'CT_DLbl' object has no attribute 'has_tx_rich'\n```\n\n## Environment\n- python-pptx version: 0.6.18\n- Python version: 3.8.5\n- OS: Windows 10\n\n<END WRITING>\n</issue>\n",
